<title>THAILAND: Official results of Nov 17 Thai general election.</title>
<headline>Official results of Nov 17 Thai general election.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Interior Ministry announced on Monday the following official results of the Thai general election held on November 17:</p>
<p>    New Aspiration Party	    125	  seats</p>
<p>    Democrat Party		    123	  seats</p>
<p>    Chart Pattana Party		52	  seats</p>
<p>    Chart Thai Party		   39	  seats</p>
<p>    Social Action Party		20	  seats</p>
<p>    Prachakorn Thai Party	    18	  seats</p>
<p>    Solidarity Party		    8	  seats</p>
<p>    Seritham Party			4	  seats</p>
<p>    Muan Chon Party		     2	  seats</p>
<p>    Palang Dharma Party		 1	  seat</p>
<p>    Thai Party			    1	  seat</p>
<p>    Thai Labour Party		 nil</p>
<p>    Free Democratic Party	   nil</p>
<p>    Total				 393	  seats</p>
<p>NOTE- A total of 62.42 percent of the 38 million eligible voters turned out to vote, the ministry said..</p>
</text>
